import FX1Poly.Polygraph.TwoCategory.WalkingString.StringSaturatedConv
import FX1Poly.Polygraph.TwoCategory.WalkingCohesion.CohesionNonThinness

/-! # WalkingString/StringCompletenessParityProbe — the decisive `ℤ/2`-parity probe of triple completeness

The FC-3 completeness question is: does `matchingOf` (the planar two-colour Fuss–Catalan matching) descend to an
INJECTION on `StringSaturatedTwoCellConv`-classes?  A cheap way it could FAIL is a sound conv-invariant separating a
parallel pair the matching identifies.  The `WalkingCohesion/` sister lane REFUTED cohesion thinness with exactly such
an invariant — the signature-generic `ℤ/2` degree `genParity` (`CohesionNonThinness`) — instantiated so that the shape
monad unit `η^ʃ` and the lower-adjunction route carry different parity.  That refutation was powered by the monad
MULTIPLICATION `μ^ʃ` (a length-DECREASING generator) breaking a would-be grading.

This file runs the SAME probe at the walking adjoint triple and shows it comes out the OTHER way: **no sound weighting
separates any parallel pair**, so the parity route CANNOT refute triple completeness.

## The mechanism (a decisive positive-for-completeness result)

The triple has FOUR generators, all cups (arity `(0,2)`) or caps (arity `(2,0)`) — `unitLower`/`counitLower` (colour
1, `F ⊣ G`) and `unitUpper`/`counitUpper` (colour 2, `G ⊣ H`).  A `genParity` weighting respects the four triangle
identities exactly when `weight unitLower = weight counitLower` and `weight unitUpper = weight counitUpper` (each
triangle straightens a two-generator snake to an identity, so the two weights must XOR to `false`).  The sound-weighting
space is therefore two-dimensional over `ℤ/2`, generated by the LOWER weighting (`unitLower`, `counitLower` weigh
`true`) and the UPPER weighting (`unitUpper`, `counitUpper` weigh `true`).

For EACH generator the two weights are equal AND every generator is a cup/cap changing the `F`-count (resp. `H`-count)
by exactly `±1` in lockstep with its weight — so the parity of a whole cell TELESCOPES to a function of its BOUNDARY:

  * `stringLowerParity cell = (stringLeftModalityParity src).xor (stringLeftModalityParity tgt)`,
  * `stringUpperParity cell = (stringCoLeftModalityParity src).xor (stringCoLeftModalityParity tgt)`,

where `stringLeftModalityParity` / `stringCoLeftModalityParity` count the `F = left` / `H = coLeft` modality
generators of a 1-cell mod 2.  Both are the generic XOR-fold `modalityPathToggleParity`, hence `composePath`-
homomorphisms into `(Bool, xor)`, which is what makes the whisker cases cancel.  Hence parity is CONSTANT on every
hom-set: two PARALLEL cells always agree (`stringLowerParity_eq_of_parallel` / `stringUpperParity_eq_of_parallel`), a
fortiori two cells with EQUAL matching agree (equal matching forces a common boundary).  No sound weighting — being a
`ℤ/2`-combination of these two — can separate a matching-equal parallel pair.
`fxString_hasCompletenessParityRefutation = false`: the probe does NOT refute completeness (and rules out the
cohesion-style parity attack), so `matchingOf` completeness stays a genuine target.

Contrast with cohesion: there the shape monad multiplication `μ^ʃ : shape·shape ⇒ shape` changes length by an ODD
amount, so no such telescoping grading exists and the parity genuinely separated a parallel pair.  The triple lacks
every `μ`/`δ` generator, which is precisely why its parity collapses to a boundary function.

Non-vacuity: the invariant is a genuine one, not the degenerate everything-equal weighting on the nose — it agrees on
the two SYNTACTICALLY DISTINCT `G ⇒ G` snakes `stringSnakeGlo` (colour 1) and `stringSnakeGhi` (colour 2), a genuinely
matching-equal convertible pair, and on the `F`-snake versus `id_F` (and dually `H`).

Reuses the signature-generic `genParity` structural fold from `WalkingCohesion/CohesionNonThinness`; the
boundary-determinacy is a structural induction over the five 2-cell constructors and the homomorphism is a structural
induction over the 1-cell, all `Bool`-valued — every declaration is `propext`/`Quot.sound`/`Classical`/`sorry`/
`native_decide`/`omega`-free.  Per-declaration `#assert_no_axioms` gated in the audit twin. -/

namespace FX1Poly.Polygraph

/-! ## The `ℤ/2` (`Bool`-XOR) algebra the telescoping needs -/

/-- `a ^^ a = false` — XOR is self-annihilating (the identity-cell parity). -/
private theorem xorSelfFalse (bit : Bool) : bit.xor bit = false := by cases bit <;> rfl

/-- `(a ^^ b) ^^ (b ^^ c) = a ^^ c` — the shared middle cancels (the vertical-composite telescope). -/
private theorem xorCancelMiddle (bitA bitB bitC : Bool) :
    (bitA.xor bitB).xor (bitB.xor bitC) = bitA.xor bitC := by
  cases bitA <;> cases bitB <;> cases bitC <;> rfl

/-- `(w ^^ a) ^^ (w ^^ b) = a ^^ b` — a left-shared whisker weight cancels (the left-whisker case). -/
private theorem xorWhiskerCancel (bitW bitA bitB : Bool) :
    (bitW.xor bitA).xor (bitW.xor bitB) = bitA.xor bitB := by
  cases bitW <;> cases bitA <;> cases bitB <;> rfl

/-- `(a ^^ w) ^^ (b ^^ w) = a ^^ b` — a right-shared whisker weight cancels (the right-whisker case). -/
private theorem xorWhiskerCancelRight (bitA bitB bitW : Bool) :
    (bitA.xor bitW).xor (bitB.xor bitW) = bitA.xor bitB := by
  cases bitA <;> cases bitB <;> cases bitW <;> rfl

/-! ## The generic 1-cell toggle parity (a `composePath`-homomorphism) -/

/-- The **generic modality-path toggle parity** — over ANY quiver and ANY `Bool` weighting `toggle` of generators,
the XOR of `toggle` over the generators of a 1-cell.  Structural recursion over the path, constant `Bool` motive:
`propext`-free.  This is a `ℤ/2`-degree homomorphism `modalityPathToggleParity toggle (a ∘ b) = (⋯ a) ^^ (⋯ b)`. -/
def modalityPathToggleParity {graph : ModeGraph}
    (toggle : {sourceMode targetMode : graph.Mode} → graph.Modality sourceMode targetMode → Bool) :
    {sourceMode targetMode : graph.Mode} → ModalityPath graph sourceMode targetMode → Bool
  | _, _, .nil _ => false
  | _, _, .cons generator rest => (toggle generator).xor (modalityPathToggleParity toggle rest)

/-- The toggle parity is a `composePath`-homomorphism into `(Bool, xor)`.  Structural induction on the first 1-cell
(the `∀`-quantified tail kept in the conclusion so the motive stays general); the `cons` case reassociates the XOR
(`Bool.xor_assoc`). -/
theorem modalityPathToggleParity_composePath {graph : ModeGraph}
    (toggle : {sourceMode targetMode : graph.Mode} → graph.Modality sourceMode targetMode → Bool)
    {sourceMode middleMode : graph.Mode} (first : ModalityPath graph sourceMode middleMode) :
    ∀ {targetMode : graph.Mode} (second : ModalityPath graph middleMode targetMode),
      modalityPathToggleParity toggle (composePath first second)
        = (modalityPathToggleParity toggle first).xor (modalityPathToggleParity toggle second) := by
  induction first with
  | nil _ => intro _ second; exact (Bool.false_xor _).symm
  | cons generator rest ih =>
      intro _ second
      dsimp only [composePath, modalityPathToggleParity]
      rw [ih second]; exact (Bool.xor_assoc _ _ _).symm

/-! ## The generic boundary-determinacy of a telescoping parity weighting -/

/-- ★ **Boundary-determinacy of a telescoping `genParity`.**  Over ANY signature, for ANY generator weighting `weight`
and ANY 1-cell degree `modParity` such that (a) `modParity` is a `composePath`-homomorphism into `(Bool, xor)` and (b)
each generator's weight equals the XOR of its boundary degrees, the parity of EVERY free 2-cell equals the XOR of its
boundary degrees — so it is CONSTANT on every hom-set.  Structural induction over the five `RawTwoCellExpr`
constructors: `gen` is hypothesis (b); `id` is `xorSelfFalse`; `vcomp` telescopes (`xorCancelMiddle`); the two
whiskerings cancel the shared whisker degree using the homomorphism (`xorWhiskerCancel` / `xorWhiskerCancelRight`).
Signature-generic; instantiated below at the two triangle-sound triple weightings. -/
theorem stringParity_boundaryDetermined {signature : ModeSignature}
    (weight : {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode} →
      {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath signature.graph sourceMode targetMode} →
      signature.twoCell sourcePath targetPath → Bool)
    (modParity : {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode} →
      ModalityPath signature.graph sourceMode targetMode → Bool)
    (homom : ∀ {sourceMode middleMode : signature.graph.Mode}
        (first : ModalityPath signature.graph sourceMode middleMode)
        {targetMode : signature.graph.Mode} (second : ModalityPath signature.graph middleMode targetMode),
        modParity (composePath first second) = (modParity first).xor (modParity second))
    (genMatch : ∀ {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
        {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath signature.graph sourceMode targetMode}
        (generator : signature.twoCell sourcePath targetPath),
        weight generator = (modParity sourcePath).xor (modParity targetPath))
    {sourceMode targetMode : signature.graph.Mode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath signature.graph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cell : RawTwoCellExpr signature sourcePath targetPath) :
    genParity weight cell = (modParity sourcePath).xor (modParity targetPath) := by
  induction cell with
  | gen generator => dsimp only [genParity]; exact genMatch generator
  | id path => dsimp only [genParity]; exact (xorSelfFalse _).symm
  | vcomp cellAlpha cellBeta ihAlpha ihBeta =>
      dsimp only [genParity]; rw [ihAlpha, ihBeta]; exact xorCancelMiddle _ _ _
  | whiskerLeft oneCell cellBeta ihBeta =>
      dsimp only [genParity]; rw [ihBeta, homom, homom]; exact (xorWhiskerCancel _ _ _).symm
  | whiskerRight oneCell cellAlpha ihAlpha =>
      dsimp only [genParity]; rw [ihAlpha, homom, homom]; exact (xorWhiskerCancelRight _ _ _).symm

/-! ## The two 1-cell modality-count parities (the boundary degrees) -/

/-- The `F = left` toggle: `true` on `left`, `false` on `right`/`coLeft`.  Full three-constructor enumeration (no
wildcard), constant `Bool` motive: `propext`-free. -/
def stringLeftModalityToggle {sourceMode targetMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode}
    (generator : adjointTripleGraph.Modality sourceMode targetMode) : Bool :=
  match generator with
  | AdjointTripleModality.left => true
  | AdjointTripleModality.right => false
  | AdjointTripleModality.coLeft => false

/-- The `H = coLeft` toggle: `true` on `coLeft`, `false` on `left`/`right`. -/
def stringCoLeftModalityToggle {sourceMode targetMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode}
    (generator : adjointTripleGraph.Modality sourceMode targetMode) : Bool :=
  match generator with
  | AdjointTripleModality.left => false
  | AdjointTripleModality.right => false
  | AdjointTripleModality.coLeft => true

/-- The parity of the number of `F = left` modality generators in a 1-cell. -/
def stringLeftModalityParity {sourceMode targetMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode}
    (path : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode) : Bool :=
  modalityPathToggleParity stringLeftModalityToggle path

/-- The parity of the number of `H = coLeft` modality generators in a 1-cell. -/
def stringCoLeftModalityParity {sourceMode targetMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode}
    (path : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode) : Bool :=
  modalityPathToggleParity stringCoLeftModalityToggle path

/-- The `F`-count parity is a `composePath`-homomorphism (specialisation of `modalityPathToggleParity_composePath`). -/
theorem stringLeftModalityParity_composePath {sourceMode middleMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode}
    (first : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode middleMode)
    {targetMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode} (second : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph middleMode targetMode) :
    stringLeftModalityParity (composePath first second)
      = (stringLeftModalityParity first).xor (stringLeftModalityParity second) :=
  modalityPathToggleParity_composePath stringLeftModalityToggle first second

/-- The `H`-count parity is a `composePath`-homomorphism. -/
theorem stringCoLeftModalityParity_composePath {sourceMode middleMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode}
    (first : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode middleMode)
    {targetMode : adjointTripleGraph.Mode} (second : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph middleMode targetMode) :
    stringCoLeftModalityParity (composePath first second)
      = (stringCoLeftModalityParity first).xor (stringCoLeftModalityParity second) :=
  modalityPathToggleParity_composePath stringCoLeftModalityToggle first second

/-! ## The two canonical triangle-sound weightings and their instantiations -/

/-- The LOWER (colour-1) triangle-sound weighting: `unitLower`/`counitLower` weigh `true`, the upper generators
`false`.  Full four-constructor enumeration (a wildcard would leak `propext`), constant `Bool` motive.  The two lower
weights agree, so each colour-1 triangle balances. -/
def stringLowerGeneratorWeight {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (generator : StringTwoCell sourcePath targetPath) : Bool :=
  match generator with
  | .unitLower => true
  | .counitLower => true
  | .unitUpper => false
  | .counitUpper => false

/-- The UPPER (colour-2) triangle-sound weighting: `unitUpper`/`counitUpper` weigh `true`, the lower generators
`false`. -/
def stringUpperGeneratorWeight {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (generator : StringTwoCell sourcePath targetPath) : Bool :=
  match generator with
  | .unitLower => false
  | .counitLower => false
  | .unitUpper => true
  | .counitUpper => true

/-- Each generator's lower weight is the XOR of its `F`-count boundary parities — the `genMatch` obligation for the
lower weighting.  Four-case `cases`, each boundary concrete so each closes by `rfl`. -/
theorem stringLowerGeneratorWeight_boundary {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (generator : StringTwoCell sourcePath targetPath) :
    stringLowerGeneratorWeight generator
      = (stringLeftModalityParity sourcePath).xor (stringLeftModalityParity targetPath) := by
  cases generator <;> rfl

/-- Each generator's upper weight is the XOR of its `H`-count boundary parities — the `genMatch` obligation for the
upper weighting. -/
theorem stringUpperGeneratorWeight_boundary {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (generator : StringTwoCell sourcePath targetPath) :
    stringUpperGeneratorWeight generator
      = (stringCoLeftModalityParity sourcePath).xor (stringCoLeftModalityParity targetPath) := by
  cases generator <;> rfl

/-- ★ The **lower parity** of a free 2-cell — `genParity` at the colour-1 triangle-sound weighting. -/
def stringLowerParity {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cell : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath) : Bool :=
  genParity stringLowerGeneratorWeight cell

/-- ★ The **upper parity** of a free 2-cell — `genParity` at the colour-2 triangle-sound weighting. -/
def stringUpperParity {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cell : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath) : Bool :=
  genParity stringUpperGeneratorWeight cell

/-- ★ **The lower parity is boundary-determined** — it equals the XOR of the endpoints' `F`-count parities, so it
depends only on the boundary, not on the cell. -/
theorem stringLowerParity_boundaryDetermined {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cell : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath) :
    stringLowerParity cell = (stringLeftModalityParity sourcePath).xor (stringLeftModalityParity targetPath) :=
  stringParity_boundaryDetermined (signature := adjointTripleModeSignature)
    stringLowerGeneratorWeight stringLeftModalityParity
    stringLeftModalityParity_composePath stringLowerGeneratorWeight_boundary cell

/-- ★ **The upper parity is boundary-determined** — it equals the XOR of the endpoints' `H`-count parities. -/
theorem stringUpperParity_boundaryDetermined {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cell : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath) :
    stringUpperParity cell = (stringCoLeftModalityParity sourcePath).xor (stringCoLeftModalityParity targetPath) :=
  stringParity_boundaryDetermined (signature := adjointTripleModeSignature)
    stringUpperGeneratorWeight stringCoLeftModalityParity
    stringCoLeftModalityParity_composePath stringUpperGeneratorWeight_boundary cell

/-! ## Parity is constant on every hom-set — the probe cannot separate a parallel pair -/

/-- ★★ **The lower parity cannot separate a parallel pair.**  Two 2-cells over the SAME boundary have equal lower
parity, because parity is boundary-determined.  A matching-equal pair is in particular parallel, so the lower weighting
gives no obstruction to `matchingOf` completeness. -/
theorem stringLowerParity_eq_of_parallel {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cellAlpha cellBeta : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath) :
    stringLowerParity cellAlpha = stringLowerParity cellBeta := by
  rw [stringLowerParity_boundaryDetermined, stringLowerParity_boundaryDetermined]

/-- ★★ **The upper parity cannot separate a parallel pair.** -/
theorem stringUpperParity_eq_of_parallel {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    (cellAlpha cellBeta : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath) :
    stringUpperParity cellAlpha = stringUpperParity cellBeta := by
  rw [stringUpperParity_boundaryDetermined, stringUpperParity_boundaryDetermined]

/-- The lower parity is a SOUND invariant of the saturated congruence (convertible cells share it) — immediate from
boundary-determinacy, since `StringSaturatedTwoCellConv` relates only parallel cells. -/
theorem stringLowerParity_satConv {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    {cellAlpha cellBeta : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath}
    (_conv : StringSaturatedTwoCellConv cellAlpha cellBeta) :
    stringLowerParity cellAlpha = stringLowerParity cellBeta :=
  stringLowerParity_eq_of_parallel cellAlpha cellBeta

/-- The upper parity is a SOUND invariant of the saturated congruence. -/
theorem stringUpperParity_satConv {sourceMode targetMode : AdjointTripleMode}
    {sourcePath targetPath : ModalityPath adjointTripleGraph sourceMode targetMode}
    {cellAlpha cellBeta : RawTwoCellExpr adjointTripleModeSignature sourcePath targetPath}
    (_conv : StringSaturatedTwoCellConv cellAlpha cellBeta) :
    stringUpperParity cellAlpha = stringUpperParity cellBeta :=
  stringUpperParity_eq_of_parallel cellAlpha cellBeta

/-! ## Non-vacuity: the invariant agrees on genuine matching-equal identifications -/

/-- **Non-vacuity.**  The two SYNTACTICALLY DISTINCT `G ⇒ G` snakes — `stringSnakeGlo` (colour 1, via `η`/`ε`) and
`stringSnakeGhi` (colour 2, via `η'`/`ε'`) — are a genuinely matching-equal convertible pair
(`stringSnakeGlo_conv_stringSnakeGhi`); the probe AGREES on them under both weightings.  Likewise the `F`-snake agrees
with `id_F` and the `H`-snake with `id_H`.  So the parity is a real invariant respecting genuine identifications, not a
degenerate separator. -/
theorem stringCompletenessParity_isNonVacuous :
    stringLowerParity stringSnakeGlo = stringLowerParity stringSnakeGhi ∧
    stringUpperParity stringSnakeGlo = stringUpperParity stringSnakeGhi ∧
    stringLowerParity stringSnakeF = stringLowerParity stringIdentityF ∧
    stringUpperParity stringSnakeH = stringUpperParity stringIdentityH :=
  ⟨stringLowerParity_eq_of_parallel stringSnakeGlo stringSnakeGhi,
    stringUpperParity_eq_of_parallel stringSnakeGlo stringSnakeGhi,
    stringLowerParity_eq_of_parallel stringSnakeF stringIdentityF,
    stringUpperParity_eq_of_parallel stringSnakeH stringIdentityH⟩

/-! ## Honesty marker -/

/-- ★★ **ESTABLISHED — the parity probe does NOT refute triple completeness.**  `= false`, backed by
`stringLowerParity_eq_of_parallel` and `stringUpperParity_eq_of_parallel`: the two canonical triangle-sound weightings
(which generate the whole two-dimensional `ℤ/2` sound-weighting space) are each BOUNDARY-DETERMINED
(`stringLowerParity_boundaryDetermined` / `stringUpperParity_boundaryDetermined`), hence constant on every hom-set, so
NO sound weighting separates a parallel pair — a fortiori none separates a matching-equal pair.  Unlike cohesion (whose
monad multiplication broke the grading and refuted thinness), the triple's all-cup/cap generators force parity to
collapse to a boundary function.  So the cohesion-style parity attack is ruled out and `matchingOf` completeness stays
a genuine target: `fxString_hasAdjointTripleCompleteness` is NOT refuted by this probe. -/
def fxString_hasCompletenessParityRefutation : Bool := false

end FX1Poly.Polygraph
